@ 29.2 - Proto-Na-Dene to Tlingit
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Wikipedia contributors (2015), “Na-Dene languages”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia. <https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Na-Dene_languages> NB: Where a colon appears, forms to the left are the typical forms and forms to the right are “l-assimilated”. Somethings going on with the velars and uvulars; apparently, both the rounded and unrounded consonants have reflexes that may or may not be rounded
	s > s : ɬ
	t͡s > t͡s : t͡ɬ
	t͡sʼ > {sʼ,t͡sʼ} : {ɬ,t͡ɬʼ}
	ʃ > {ʃ,s} : ɬ
	t͡ʃ > {t͡ʃ,t͡s} : t͡ɬ
	t͡ʃʼ > {sʼ,t͡ʃʼ} : t͡ɬʼ
	kʲ kʲʼ > {k,ʃ} kʼ
	xʲ > x
	kʷʼ > {x,k}ʷʼ
	xʷ > x
	qʼ qʷʼ > χʷʼ {χʼ,qʷʼ}
	x > ∅ / {s,ʃ}_
	$ > χ